{
	"_comment": [
		"Budgets of the perf tests (StrataTests/src/Perf, suites Perf.* and PerfGPU.*; AGENTS.md, 'Testing').",
		"Every metric a test checks (Perf::CheckBudgetConfirmed, CheckBudgetsConfirmed) or records (Perf::Record) needs an",
		"entry, or the test fails:",
		"  \"<Suite>.<Metric>\": { \"Measured\": <number>, \"Budget\": <number>, \"Unit\": <unit>, \"Target\": <number> }",
		"with a unit of \"ms\", \"us\", \"MB\", \"count\" or \"ratio\" (of two measurements, e.g. a new way's time to an old",
		"way's). Lower is better: a test fails when it measures more than Budget in every attempt of its confirmed check",
		"(express rates as cost per item). Measured is the metric on the reference machine (Intel Core i7-13700K, NVIDIA",
		"GeForce RTX 5090, Windows 11, Release build, ctest --preset windows-release -L perf on a quiet machine); Budget is",
		"at most 1.5 times Measured (round down), or an acceptance limit below that.",
		"Target (optional) is a roadmap goal below Budget that the metric has not reached on every run: the budget is the",
		"gate, the target is reported with every check. A budget lowered to its target or below drops the target.",
		"Limits that tests check belong here, never in the test's code.",
		"Ratchet: budgets only go down. A change that makes a metric cheaper measures it again and lowers Measured and",
		"Budget in the same commit; a metric over its budget is a regression to fix, never a reason to raise the budget.",
		"A commit that adds or lowers a budget states the measured values in its message."
	],
